## Publish later on GitHub Pages

Upload `index.html`, `styles.css`, `content.js`, `script.js`, `.nojekyll`, and the `assets` directory to the root of a GitHub repository. In Settings → Pages choose Deploy from a branch, select the branch and `/ (root)`. All asset paths are relative, including for repository subpaths. The `src` source-notes folder is not needed for deployment.
